Laden OS installs with Calamares 3.4.2, built by scripts/build-calamares.sh.
Arch does not ship that package. The window is started by laden-install.

Calamares 3.4 does not read an ignored-disk list. laden-install writes
/run/laden-os/install-ignored, and the patched partition scan refuses every
disk in that file. A missing file refuses every disk. Identity matches
(the Acer Hynix drive, the Kingston system disk, and a volume label of Acer)
are also set read-only before the window opens. The disk the machine is
running from is left writable and is still refused as a target.

An installed system must not keep live autologin, the live sudoers rule,
or the live polkit rule. shellprocess.conf removes those after the copy.
